data.content:
## Breaking Changes in Microsoft.OpenApi v2 (shipped with .NET 10)

The `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 package upgraded from OpenApi v1 → v2. Here's what broke and how to fix it:

| Issue | v1 (.NET 9) | v2 (.NET 10) |
|-------|-------------|--------------|
| Primitive values | `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. | `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` |
| Nullable | `schema.Nullable = true` | `schema.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| References | `obj.Reference = new OpenApiReference{...}` | Use `OpenApiSchemaReference` / `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference` wrapper types |
| `ReferenceType` enum | `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` | Removed; type is implicit in the reference class |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` | `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>` | Has `Scheme` and `Scopes` properties |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { Scheme = oAuthScheme, Scopes = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null; // remove Null flag
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of changes:
1. **`OpenApiString` → `JsonValue.Create(...)`** — all `OpenApiAny` types replaced by `JsonNode`.
2. **`OpenApiSecurityScheme` + `OpenApiReference`** → **`OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("id")`** — references are now strongly-typed wrappers.
3. **`new() { [scheme] = scopes }`** → **`new() { Scheme = ..., Scopes = ... }`** — `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a dictionary.
4. **`Nullable = false`** → **`Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null`** — nullable is a flag on `Type`, not a separate property.
